A||||7||Eric||Lighten my load||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||12-11-2000||12:45 AM||||Would some of you experts tell me how to lighten my car without comprimising saftey and comfort?  I have a heavy Fiero.  She's on a strict diet of 89 octane and semi-synthetic Valvoline, but I'm afraid there are still pounds to be shed.  Can someone (1FST2M6) tell me how to get a pig like mine down to a feather-like weight of say 2600lbs? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||12-11-2000||02:52 AM||||Take out everything you don't need  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>AC, spare tire, jack, trunk carpet, windsheild washer fluid resevoir, power locks, passenger seat, heat sheilds, etc etc...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||maninblack||12-11-2000||09:43 AM||||and also like most race driver,have a good diet yourself.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-11-2000||10:44 AM||||the seats make a big difference too.. went from the 28lb stock one to 11.8lb corbeaus.. ditch the carpet pading.. (leave the carpet though). ALL the heat sheilding (except the one on the slave cyl) the blower for the engine bay.. most don't work anyway, the a/c, line compressor, bracketry, all the crap up front a/c related. the e-brake and all it's components. (sorry jeff but i wanted it fast..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) stay with the 14" wheels for a tighter rotating mass. or a set of panasport superlights (168ea at paul Spruell Alfa, Lotus, Lambo.) uum lets see.. the guage pod.. replace them with autometer... saves about 9oz.. (not really worth the money for weight but looks sweet and is more accurate) the a/c lines that run the length of the car.. the black 1lb piece of plastic that centers the fuel pump and hinders the flow, easily removed. (in the tank) all the insulation in the engine bay. i can keep going.. the steering dampener. cross drill the rotors. the stock exhaust.. replace it with a flowmaster or other chambered unit.. save a few pounds.. the packed on weight more than stock and don't last as long.  of course the obvious.. spare, jack, tire iron. battery to Optima or Orbital drycell (45lb) instead of the 60lb wet cell.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||GeeDee86GT||12-11-2000||02:46 PM||||Try lifting a Fiero door with all the innner and outer panels still attached. But then, I have a hernia already.<P>Gary<BR>http:www.geocities.com/garby_d||||reg||9
Z||000005||Tigger||12-11-2000||03:12 PM||||You could always get rid of the drivers seat too. j/k<P>I drove mine without one from the front yard to the backyard.  Pretty interesting sitting on the floorboard, trying put your feet UP to the pedals and shift.  I should have taken pics  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000006||ChadMan||12-11-2000||03:32 PM||||Simple, Eric...trade me your GT for my 88 Coupe.  No heavy power options or A/C compressor to weigh you down.  I don't even have that heavy rear sway bar or cast-iron V6 adding extra weight.||||reg||10
Z||000007||bubbajoexx||12-11-2000||06:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B>Would some of you experts tell me how to lighten my car without comprimising saftey and comfort?  I have a heavy Fiero.  She's on a strict diet of 89 octane and semi-synthetic Valvoline, but I'm afraid there are still pounds to be shed.  Can someone (1FST2M6) tell me how to get a pig like mine down to a feather-like weight of say 2600lbs? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>unless the car is loaded with optoins it should only weigh 2560 to start with.||||reg||1
